Subject: Goldfish: read common rules text, cast creatures that carry removal

The solo test modeled a card only when the whole card was one shape (a
land, a mana rock, a "Draw N" spell, a land-ramp spell, equipment with a
bonus, a creature with nothing but keywords). Everything else was cast as a
blank body, and anything with removal, a board wipe, a counterspell, a
sacrifice or life-payment cost, a coin flip or a hybrid mana cost was never
cast at all, creatures included. Measured on Scryfall's oracle cards
(2026-10-21): 10.8% of the 32,116 Commander-legal cards were modeled.

This patch:

- adds mystic_forge/goldfish/rules_text.py, which reads a card sentence by
  sentence into the existing annotation vocabulary (no new verbs): enter,
  cast, upkeep, attack, combat, spell-cast, creature/land/equipment-enter
  triggers with draw, gain life, Treasure, creature tokens, damage or life
  loss to opponents, +1/+1 counters, self pumps, basic-land ramp, tutors,
  rituals, extra combats; anthems, extra land drops, cost reductions, token
  doubling; tapped and mana-cost activated abilities; prowess. Each sentence
  is read, has no effect in a goldfish game (evasion, "can't block", death
  triggers: nothing blocks or dies), is interaction with nothing to hit, or
  is unknown. The output goes through validate_annotations like any client
  annotation. Approximations carry notes (lifelink life not counted,
  kicker/cycling/flashback not used, scry does not reorder, monarch drawn at
  upkeep, and so on);
- a card with no unknown sentence is auto-annotated; a permanent whose
  interaction has nothing to hit is cast and counted in that out-of-scope
  class (Derived.aside_class, used by _goldfish_prepare's card_scopes); a
  spell whose whole effect is interaction stays uncast, as before; a card
  with an unknown sentence still needs annotation but plays what was read
  (Derived.unread lists the rest, and goldfish_annotate shows both);
- a sentence that limits the others and is not read ("Activate only once
  each turn", "This ability triggers only once each turn", "If you do",
  a keyword label such as Boast or Exhaust whose limit is in its reminder
  text) keeps the read parts from playing: such a card is a body that
  asks for a model, so no limit is silently dropped; only real ability
  words (Landfall, Raid, ...) are stripped as labels;
- permanents that _d9_class set aside (sacrifice and life-payment costs,
  coin flips) are now cast and asked for instead of never cast;
- hybrid and Phyrexian costs are paid with their first colour (noted)
  instead of the card never being cast;
- the engine reads double strike (combat damage twice, nothing blocks) and
  defender (never attacks);
- tests/goldfish/test_known_answers.py: hand-worked kill turns (a commander
  with 99 Mountains: plain, double strike, haste, defender, an anthem and an
  enter-the-battlefield drain read from text) and the reading of real cards'
  oracle text. test_unmodeled_other_patterns is updated to the new pin.

Measured with the same oracle file: 16.1% of Commander-legal cards fully
modeled (35.0% weighted by EDHREC rank), and on Forge's 85 Commander
precons from 2023 to 2026, 51.4% of each deck's cards played with their
effect on average, up from 34.5%.

Upstream: Kautiontape/mystic-forge at dd82cd1 (main, 2026-10-03) has no
such reader. Needs patches 0001-0008 applied first.

